# Deliberately empty. This file shadows /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/85-brltty.rules.
#
# brltty is the braille display daemon Ubuntu installs by default. It claims
# USB-serial adapters that share a VID:PID with braille hardware -- CH340
# (1a86:7523) among them -- and this is the single most common way a CH340
# project fails on modern Ubuntu: /dev/ttyUSB0 appears at boot, then vanishes a
# few seconds later when brltty grabs it. The kiosk sees the MDB reader
# disappear for no visible reason, which looks exactly like the USB fault the
# error-31 work is chasing.
#
# udev resolves rule files by name, and /etc wins over /usr/lib, so an empty
# file here disables brltty's rules outright. That is the intent: a kiosk has
# no braille display attached.
#
# install.sh also masks brltty.service and brltty-udev.service. If you would
# rather not have the package at all:
#
#     sudo apt-get purge brltty
#
# Deleting this file restores stock brltty behaviour.
